{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-phone-tracker-services-2-b-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-4","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-services-2","refs":["F-phone-618","FN-B-alerts-phone-tracker-lib-b-01"],"severity":"S3","title":"When a trainer changes a plan, any exercise the member once changed silently keeps the member's old version, and neither side is told","what":"A member who tapped 'Update routine?' after a workout (for example added a set) has changed that gym routine on the phone. When the trainer later sends a new version of the plan, those changed rows keep the member's version and skip the trainer's change. The phone works out which routines kept the member's version, then throws that list away: the member gets 'Your gym changed your workout plan' and sees no change on those exercises, and the trainer believes the new plan is what the member is doing.","expected":"After a gym plan update, the member is told which exercises kept their own version (with a way to take the trainer's), or the trainer can see the member's copy differs from what was sent.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/gymPlansSync.ts:6-7","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/gymPlansSync.ts:120","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/routineMerge.ts:9-10","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/routineMerge.ts:343","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/routineMerge.ts:380","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/routineOffer.ts:118-120"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"gym-plan-kept-edits-discarded","who":"members following a gym plan, and their trainers","how_often":"every plan update after the member changed that routine","fix_line":"Show the member which exercises kept their own version after a gym plan update, with a one-tap 'Use trainer's version'","fix_size":"medium","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-phone-tracker-services-2-b-02","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-3","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-services-2","refs":["F-phone-631","FN-L16-phone-tracker-services-2-02"],"severity":"S4","title":"When the phone cannot ask the watch to open at a workout start, nothing records it","what":"Starting a workout asks the watch app to open on its own. If that request fails on the phone side, the error is swallowed with no note at all, so a member who says 'my watch never opens' leaves nothing to look at.","expected":"A failed request to open the watch leaves a short tagged note in the phone's log, as the other watch requests already do.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/watchOpen.ts:35-40","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restCard.ts:266-268","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/restCard.ts:545-553"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"watch-open-failure-not-logged","who":"members with a watch","how_often":"rare, when the request fails","fix_line":"Log a tagged line when the open-watch request fails","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
